# jemdoc: menu{MENU}{latex.html}
= jemdocx -- equations

jemdocx renders TeX-style mathematics with MathJax 4 by default. MathJax runs
in the browser, produces scalable output, and does not require a local TeX
installation during site generation.

== Inline equations
Dollar signs surround inline mathematics. The source
+$f^\star(y) = \sup_x(y^Tx - f(x))$+ produces
$f^\star(y) = \sup_x(y^Tx - f(x))$ in a paragraph.

== Display equations
Classic jemdoc uses +\(+ and +\)+ on separate lines for display equations:

~~~
{Syntax}{}
\(
  (I \+ XY)^{-1} = I - X(I \+ YX)^{-1}Y
\)
~~~

The result is

\(
  (I + XY)^{-1} = I - X(I + YX)^{-1}Y.
\)

== Selecting a backend
Choose the renderer on the command line:

~~~
{}{sh}
python3 jemdoc --math mathjax page.jemdoc
python3 jemdoc --math png page.jemdoc
python3 jemdoc --math none page.jemdoc
~~~

The same choice can be made per document in the first-line options:

~~~
{Syntax}{}
\# jemdoc: math{png}
~~~

The +png+ backend preserves the original jemdoc behavior. It requires +latex+
and +dvipng+, writes images under the configured equation directory, and honors
the existing +eqsize+, +eqdir+, +addpackage+, +addtex+, and +noeqcache+
modelines. These options do not affect MathJax output.

Use +math{none}+ or +--math none+ when another layer will process the original
equation markup.
